// Collège (A2) — Travel, London, past simple and comparatives
$CATEGORY: College/Anglais

::Yesterday::Choose the correct form. Yesterday we ___ to the British Museum.{=went ~go ~goes ~going}

::How much::How much ___ a ticket for the London Eye?{=is ~are ~does ~has}

::Going to::We are going ___ visit Big Ben tomorrow.{=to ~for ~at ~in}

::Buses::There ___ many red buses in London.{=are ~is ~has ~have}

::Bigger::London is ___ than Brighton.{=bigger ~more big ~biggest ~big}

::The Tube::In London, people often call the underground railway…{=the Tube ~the Pipe ~the Line ~the Cab}

::A map::Can I ___ a map, please?{=have ~to have ~having ~had}

::Turn left::"Turn left" means "tourne à gauche".{T}
